{"id":"mongol-rally","title":"Mongol Rally","who":"The Adventurists · since 2004","when":"Every summer (launch in July)","vehicle":"A small, unsuitable car (classically under 1.2 litres)","kind":"rally","color":"#ca8a04","summary":"Not a race and no route: a start in Europe, a finish in Asia, and whatever crazy way teams choose in between, in cars that should never leave the city, raising money for charity. Teams launch from the UK or Czechia, converge on Prague, then head through Istanbul, the Caucasus and Central Asia (or Russia), often meeting in Samarkand, before Mongolia. The finish moved from Ulaanbaatar to Ulan-Ude in Siberia, and in 2025 to Oskemen in Kazakhstan. About 13,000–16,000 km in three to four weeks.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Mongol Rally","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_Rally"},{"label":"The Adventurists: Mongol Rally guide","url":"https://www.theadventurists.com/guides/mongol-rally/"},{"label":"WeRoad: Mongol Rally 2026, route and dates","url":"https://www.weroad.it/blog/mongol-rally-cosa-e-percorso-date"}],"approximate":"One classic southern route through the Caucasus and Central Asia to the old finish in Ulaanbaatar and on to Ulan-Ude; every team picks its own way.","km":13664,"bbox":[-1.6162,39.6554,107.5839,52.0823],"stops":[{"name":"Goodwood","place":"Goodwood Circuit, England","at":[50.8597,-0.7581],"text":"The classic British launch: a lap of the circuit, then east.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Circuit_de_Goodwood_-_logo.jpg/500px-Circuit_de_Goodwood_-_logo.jpg","page":"Goodwood Circuit","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Circuit_de_Goodwood_-_logo.jpg","credit":"Y.Leclercq©","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Prague","place":"Praha, Czechia","at":[50.0875,14.4213],"text":"The launch party where teams converge (the 2026 start was in Czechia).","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Prague_%286365119737%29.jpg/500px-Prague_%286365119737%29.jpg","page":"Prague","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prague_%286365119737%29.jpg","credit":"Moyan Brenn from Italy","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Istanbul","place":"Istanbul, Turkey","at":[41.0064,28.9759],"text":"Across the Balkans to the Bosphorus.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg/500px-Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","page":"Istanbul","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_peninsula_and_modern_skyline_of_Istanbul.jpg","credit":"Hunanuk","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"Tbilisi","place":"Tbilisi, Georgia","at":[41.6935,44.8014],"text":"Into the Caucasus.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/View_of_Tbilisi_from_Tabori_Church_2023-10-08-2.jpg/500px-View_of_Tbilisi_from_Tabori_Church_2023-10-08-2.jpg","page":"Tbilisi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Tbilisi_from_Tabori_Church_2023-10-08-2.jpg","credit":"Alexey Komarov","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Baku","place":"Baku, Azerbaijan","at":[40.3756,49.8328],"text":"Waiting days for a cargo ferry over the Caspian.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Baku_city_at_night.jpg/500px-Baku_city_at_night.jpg","page":"Baku","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baku_city_at_night.jpg","credit":"Presidential Press and Information Office","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Aktau","place":"Aktau, Kazakhstan","at":[43.6353,51.1682],"text":"Off the boat into the Kazakh steppe.","by":"ferry"},{"name":"Nukus","place":"Nukus, Uzbekistan","at":[42.46,59.6177],"text":"Terrible roads past the dried-up Aral Sea.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Berdaq_at%C4%B1nda%C7%B5%C4%B1_Qaraqalpaq_%C3%A1debiyat%C4%B1_tariyx%C4%B1_m%C3%A1mleketlik_muzeyi.jpg/500px-Berdaq_at%C4%B1nda%C7%B5%C4%B1_Qaraqalpaq_%C3%A1debiyat%C4%B1_tariyx%C4%B1_m%C3%A1mleketlik_muzeyi.jpg","page":"Nukus","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berdaq_at%C4%B1nda%C7%B5%C4%B1_Qaraqalpaq_%C3%A1debiyat%C4%B1_tariyx%C4%B1_m%C3%A1mleketlik_muzeyi.jpg","credit":"Aziko9","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"Samarkand","place":"Samarkand, Uzbekistan","at":[39.655,66.9757],"text":"Where the southern and northern routes often meet.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/RegistanSquare_Samarkand.jpg/500px-RegistanSquare_Samarkand.jpg","page":"Registan","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RegistanSquare_Samarkand.jpg","credit":"Registan_-_Gusjer.jpg: Gustavo Jeronimo from Aranjuez, Spain derivative work: MrPanyGoff","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Almaty","place":"Almaty, Kazakhstan","at":[43.2364,76.9457],"text":"North-east along the Tian Shan.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Almaty_K%C3%B6k_T%C3%B6be.jpg/500px-Almaty_K%C3%B6k_T%C3%B6be.jpg","page":"Almaty","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almaty_K%C3%B6k_T%C3%B6be.jpg","credit":"Dauren Nabijan","license":"CC0"}},{"name":"Oskemen","place":"Oskemen, Kazakhstan","at":[49.9484,82.6275],"text":"The 2025 finish, in East Kazakhstan.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/%D0%9F%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%A3%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%81%D0%BA.jpg/500px-%D0%9F%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%A3%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%81%D0%BA.jpg","page":"Oskemen","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9F%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B0_%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%B0_%D0%A3%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C-%D0%9A%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%81%D0%BA.jpg","credit":"Andriej Szypiłow","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},